v0.9b4 2026-09-17
- No energy-accounting algorithm changes from v0.9b2/v0.9b3.
- Replaced the hard Venus v3.79/exact-SHA install lock with fail-closed structural compatibility checks for later Venus OS versions.
- Added firstCompatibleVersion v3.79; known hashes now identify actually validated sources rather than the only allowed sources.
- Unknown upstream files may be patched only with zero fuzz; forward and reverse must succeed, reverse must restore the source byte-for-byte, expected package markers must occur exactly once, and all patched Python must compile.
- Added tools/preflight.sh for live compatibility checks before installation/reinstallation.
- Added tools/feature.sh as the supported A/B control for Fix 3 and Fix 4; it updates persistent config and restarts only the required service.
- Documented that legacy Node-RED/state-file controls are not connected to this package and should be removed after migration.
- Clarified that a structurally compatible future Venus version is not considered field-validated until regression tests are performed.

v0.9b3 2026-09-16
- No energy-accounting algorithm changes from v0.9b2.
- Added deterministic vrmlogger restart verification after install/uninstall.
- Made the default configuration fail-safe for reuse on other systems: optional features disabled and no DeviceInstance overrides.
- Clarified the SetupHelper 9.4 firmware-update reinstall path and fail-closed behavior on unvalidated Venus/source versions.
- Added a status helper for quick maintenance checks.
- Moved the one-off manual-patch migration utility under tools/legacy so it is not confused with normal installation.

v0.9b2 2026-09-16
- Fixed validation on Venus OS: use SetupHelper's full patch utility instead of BusyBox patch.
- Validation now mirrors SetupHelper forward/reverse patch handling with separate output files.

v0.9b1 2026-09-16
- Consolidated four logical fixes into one SetupHelper package.
- Removed Node-RED/state-file control for authoritative AC load meter.
- Moved runtime settings to persistent SetupHelper options config.
- Removed duplicated VE.Bus input-role logic; Fix 2 and Fix 4 now share one resolver.
- Clarified cross-VE.Bus matching as sampling-interval based, not globally simultaneous.
- Added strict v3.79/base-hash validation and Python compile preflight.
- Documented tested and untested scenarios, Base Load behavior and meter scope requirements.
